The introduction of the crowding agent 20 wt% Ficoll leads also to the formation of additional peaks in the E-histograms for the DNA Hp (Figure 6E). Peak maxima are recorded at E = 0.13 ± 0.01, 0.31 ± 0.01, 0.60 ± 0.01 and 0.85 ± 0.01, pointing to an even more rugged conformational landscape of the DNA Hp. In case of 20 wt% Ficoll, the single-molecule fluorescence traces display mostly two-state dynamics as shown in Supplementary Figure S14. We may consider the two-state dynamics in terms of folded and unfolded states with a bimodal FRET distribution each. The FRET distribution in case of the folded state is centered at E = 0.60 ± 0.01 and 0.85 ± 0.01, and that of the unfolded state at E = 0.13 ± 0.01, 0.31 ± 0.01, respectively. The dwell times were corrected for the increased viscosity in 20 wt% Ficoll solution and used to determine the folding (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
